# Intro
Reproduces STARBENCH's (Bisbas et al. 2015, MNRAS 453, 1324, arXiv:1507.05621) late-phase D-type expansion test: a single ionizing source at the center of a uniform pure-hydrogen medium (`n_H ~ 3115 cm^-3`, `Q_H = 1e49` photons/s). Validated against STARBENCH's own semi-empirical solution (Eqns 8, 11, 28, 29 -- a blend of the pressure-driven and shell-inertia ODEs), not the classical Spitzer (1978) formula the sibling `../StromgrenSphere/` example uses (Spitzer over-predicts at late times, the whole reason STARBENCH exists). Use `starbench_analytic_check.py`, not `stromgren_analytic_check.py`.

## Temperature
STARBENCH assumes a flat `T_i=1e4 K` / `T_o=1e3 K` two-temperature medium. This code computes `T_i` from metallicity instead; at `Z=0` (this example's default) it gives `T_i~47500 K`. To match STARBENCH's own convention, build with the flag below. `SPH:minimal_temperature=1000` floors the neutral gas at `T_o` regardless of build (already set in `params.yml`).

## Star mass
`star_mass=26.75 Msun` gives `Q_H=1e49 s^-1` in this code's mass-luminosity fit (`radiation_get_individual_star_ionizing_photon_emission_rate_fit`, `src/feedback/GEAR/radiation.c`).

## Resolution
`gas_mass=0.1 Msun` (default), ~770k particles.

## Box size
`boxsize=0.01` kpc (10 pc). Sized for the `T_i=1e4 K` build, where `R_STAG` stays inside the box for the full 3 Myr run. At the plain build's natural `T_i~47500 K`, `R_STAG` exceeds the box; `starbench_analytic_check.py` automatically limits its comparison window to when the analytic prediction is still box-valid.

## Gravity
`--external-gravity` is passed but no `Potential:` block is set, so there is no gravitational force -- matching STARBENCH's own purely hydrodynamical test.

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_0 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j
```
To match STARBENCH's own `T_i=1e4 K` convention instead of this code's natural metallicity-dependent value, add `CFLAGS+="-DIONIZATION_FEEDBACK_DEBUG_FIXED_IONIZED_TEMPERATURE_K=1e4"` before `./configure`.

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Override any parameter via the matching env var, e.g. `gas_mass=0.05 ./run.sh` -- see `run.sh` for the full list.

# Checking
```
python3 starbench_analytic_check.py -s "snap/snapshot_*.hdf5"
```
Pass `--T-ionized-K 1e4` (matching whatever `T_i` the build used) if built with the flag above.
